A||||1||88formula||Update on my 3.4-liter engine rebuild and compression ratio||||1||
Z||000000||88formula||01-18-2001||08:21 PM||||I just talked to my machinist about my motor. If you guys don't know I am rebuilding a high performance 3.4-liter engine. I am using the pistons from the Twin cam 3.4-liter engine in my OHV engine to raise the compression ratio from the stock 9.0-1 to a hopefully healthier 9.7-1. I am going the have the volume measured on the combustion chambers and the valve relief’s so we can figure out what the compression ratio is actually going to be. According the many sources it is supposed to be 9.7-1. He also ported the heads and performed a multi angle valve jog for me and installed ARP head bolts, rod bolts, and main studs in the engine. Many other things were done also. <P>According to Dyno2000 and Drastrip2000 this 5-speed formula will have 209 horsepower @ 5500 rpm and 237-ft. lbs. of torque @ 4000 rpm. It will get to 60 mph in 5.5 seconds and run the quarter mile in 13.8 seconds @ 98.2 mph with the right conditions and it is naturally aspired. Man I can’t wait to get this thing running for the summer.  <P>Pictures of the engine rebuild will come.  <BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||01-19-2001||04:56 AM||||Sounds awesome!  Keep a good journal so I can copy your work  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||
